{
  "requirement": "With `--dry-run`, `habeas refactor` MUST report every change it would make,\nin the same form as {cite}`requirements.refactor.command`, and MUST write\nnothing.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.refactor.dry_run` imposes three obligations. With `--dry-run`, `habeas refactor` MUST report every change it would make. It MUST report in the same form as `requirements.refactor.command`, which lists changed records and unchanged records with reasons. It MUST write nothing. I found tests and assertions for each.\n\n**Writes nothing.**\n- `tests/refactor.rs#fn[a_dry_run_reports_the_same_changes_and_writes_nothing]` builds a project, moves `load` to a new file, and snapshots the whole tree with `snapshot`. It runs `--dry-run`, asserts success, and asserts the snapshot is unchanged.\n- `snapshot` reads every file under the root, so any rewritten or newly created file would be caught.\n- `tests/refactor.rs#fn[versioned_records_preserve_sdk_dependencies_across_verified_moves]` repeats the unchanged-snapshot assertion for seven scenarios: `rename`, `move`, `selector`, `file`, `edit`, `extra` and `bad-extra`. These cover a requirement rename, a code-node move, a selector change, a file move, and records that cannot be migrated.\n\n**Reports every change, in the same form as the real run.**\n- Both tests run the real command after the dry run and compare outputs. The only differences allowed are the dry-run wording (\"Would rewrite\", \"Would change\", \"Would leave\") against the real-run wording (\"Rewrote\", \"Changed\", \"Left\").\n- A dry run that omitted a rewrite or a changed record, or that listed it in a different form, would fail the equality assertion.\n- The comparison covers \"left unchanged\" entries too. In the `edit` and `bad-extra` scenarios, the real output is asserted to contain \"Left 1 records unchanged\", and the dry-run output is asserted to equal it after the word substitution. This covers the unchanged-with-reason half of the `command` form.\n- The scenarios also cover reference rewrites in directives and sources (`rename`, `extra`) and evidence-record migration, so the report is checked in more than one change class.\n\n**Unspecified details.** The exact \"Would …\" wording is not specified by the requirement, so the word-substitution comparison is a reasonable way to check \"same form\". Behavior on invalid mappings is a `requirements.refactor.command` concern and is not part of this subject.\n\nI found no gap.",
